  "id": "DrugBank_DB00515 - MONDO_6335",
  "verbalization": "Cisplatin is implicated in the progression of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through a series of indirect pathways, primarily through the Indication links to Immature Ovarian Teratoma and Melphalan. These intermediaries suggest a potential role for Cisplatin in the treatment or pathogenesis of this cancer, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of Tretamine as an intermediate in another pathway adds another layer of complexity, highlighting the possibility of multiple pathways involving Cisplatin in the context of ovarian cancer. The evidence suggests that Cisplatin may influence the development or progression of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through interactions with other entities, possibly via metabolic or signaling pathways that are not directly specified in the provided data. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering both direct and indirect relationships in understanding the role of Cisplatin in ovarian cancer.",
